{"title":"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Newton’s method applied to the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0df624702c1f988d1b966737e9c46c03bd39eb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x^3-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"19\" /> takes the form of the iteration <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/8885a96b8f00b77a367c1a24db191d1cedf738e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1} =x_n-\\frac{(x_n)^3-x_n}{3{x_n}^2-1} , n = 0,1,2,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"303\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>(a) What are the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57ccf8d123ba4259e29fba55d9b008874e071492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />? \n</p><p>(b) Study the behavior of the iteration when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/3/313f1bc49fedd53375f2bf1392783230cea7989a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0 &gt; \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"68\" height=\"41\" /> to conclude that the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/69551c3500bc3d72e8da62cb464c89b4ff8c54c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_0,x_1,\\ldots\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> approaches the same root as long as you choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/3/313f1bc49fedd53375f2bf1392783230cea7989a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0 &gt; \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"68\" height=\"41\" />. It may be helpful to start with the case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc271598aa425b1f006e6db4fa5dfa0e90f8e7e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>(c) Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904d8adba8430da264ef4946399ec7e14486a035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\alpha &lt; x_0 &lt; \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />. For what number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> does the sequence always approach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p>(d) For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/b/36bb2bc18eebc8db8e9490c2526747cc79ee10c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0 \\in(\\alpha,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"100\" height=\"41\" /> the sequence may approach either of the roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9c7695aa4cd5bf92c7da668b766fdfe244a113a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm x^{*}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" />. Can you ﬁnd an (implicit) expression that can be used to determine limits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac5179cf12e1a7ff085b57db0ca3f9d9c2e6e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> such that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/2/6129d38d496e99f6410e09e6e0d18f42257c4034.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x0 \\in (a_i,a_{i+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" /> then the sequence approaches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/4/5549be72a072b90b44c61e9f513388766bc6f199.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1)^i{x^{*}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"19\" />. Hint:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8fe8abbe2edf8c2677bc17eb0a981830eb12397.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}, a_i &gt; a_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"146\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> approaches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae26d1d19e9371dd57975f8cc1eb7c580626ad25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"30\" height=\"43\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> becomes large.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(a) The roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6f73ce3de3a556fbdbb2bfa9cf08647141c88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1,0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>(b) First consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/b/8fbf8de2bd82a42be77eca6ebd0e4858f07d407f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0 &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd80e269a889a13f7ddba37ac9cd6d0e389a9e76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1} = 1 + \\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/f/b3f8912e908a95f347df18bd4f173f543725ce95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n = 1 + \\delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/4/9a4b1ee77622f50ac112610b5be1c8feb031ef31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\delta &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />. The iteration gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc66a9838200e0f7e88b8e2d1b628748dfde8be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt;\\frac{\\epsilon}{\\delta} &lt; \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"85\" height=\"38\" />. Next consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/8/388d7a1c5058b8ac3043f3bc812032e6dae6c998.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} &lt; x_0 &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"102\" height=\"41\" />. As the signs of the numerator and denominator in the rational part of the iteration does not change on the interval under consideration we ﬁnd that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/3/943423ec3372bca69f75b40263088442dcc5bb47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />. Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcb3fc2febb1988b36512463c821633812603961.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/d/2dd241834905de5246fcbb2444ed65f963fccbce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>To answer (c), rewrite the iteration as<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/4/5e4867baa889604a33aaf90b69649de3b0b88e70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1} =-\\frac{2(x_n)^3}{1-3(x_n)^2 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"158\" height=\"43\" />, and note that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/a/47a4132741dfe1052b6c8ed959632cebe27f4f81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;=x_0 &lt; \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"116\" height=\"41\" /> the next iterate will be non-positive. Insisting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/a/cbad59d37e162bb2f0868b90d3bee04b27e6a8fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-x_0 &lt; x_1 &lt;= 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> will be closer to zero than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f1249ad95b7682b8316ad21de8ce4ee9fdcf93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> gives the limiting case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/6/b360234ae2bbb82df12770589d1a294c6b1c93ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 =-x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"10\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/e/67e03106e65bee7b0a8257ffeb70b6cfb4b6bee4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha (1-3\\alpha^2) =-2\\alpha^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"19\" />, which has the solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/e/56e994a290056846abd386e762bdc222f22b9872.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"62\" height=\"41\" />. \n</p><p>Finally the implicit recurrence in (d) is obtained by running Newton backwards\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f6090d300271cfb6549bb263a345b2c3a59ce55e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i-\\frac{a_i^3-a_i}{3a_i^2-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"97\" height=\"43\" />  = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/0/390660a9dd7c446ba72143385691e20feb8fd5eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-a_{i-1}, a_1 = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}},\\ldots,a_{\\infty}= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"239\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II\">2017 UNM-PNM Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://mathcontest.unm.edu/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest\" title=\"UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest\"> All UNM-PNM Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018004043\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.040 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 257/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1820/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 105/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7610/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.193      1 Template:UNM-PNM_Math_Contest_box\n100.00%    7.193      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17128:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018004043 and revision id 100618. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}